ad -- Constructs the standard matrix representation of the adjoint operator
***************************************************************************

Description
===========

The matrices constructed by this can get very large.



+-----------------------------------------+
|i1 : ea = exteriorExtension(3, 7, e, QQ);|
+-----------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = ea.ad(first ea.bases#1);        |
|                                         |
|              174       174              |
|o2 : Matrix QQ    <-- QQ                 |
+-----------------------------------------+
|i3 : rank A                              |
|                                         |
|o3 = 46                                  |
+-----------------------------------------+

This rank is an invariant

See also
========

  * *note powerRanks: powerRanks, -- Compute the ranks of powers of a matrix
  * *note powerTraces: powerTraces, -- Compute the traces of powers of a matrix
  * *note blockPowerRanks: blockPowerRanks, -- Computes a list of ranks of
    blocks for each power of a matrix representation of an adjoint operator for
    ExteriorExtensions
  * *note prettyBlockPowerRanks: prettyBlockPowerRanks, -- same as
    blockPowerRanks, but prettier
  * *note getBlock: getBlock, -- Extract a block of the matrix representation
    of an adjoint operator for ExteriorExtensions

For the programmer
==================

The object *note ad: ad, is a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

