powerRanks -- Compute the ranks of powers of a matrix
*****************************************************

Description
===========

This is what you do:



+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : ea = exteriorExtension(3, 6, QQ);|
+--------------------------------------+
|i2 : A = ea.ad(first ea.bases#1);     |
|                                      |
|              55       55             |
|o2 : Matrix QQ   <-- QQ               |
+--------------------------------------+
|i3 : ea.powerRanks A                  |
|                                      |
|o3 = {20, 1, 0}                       |
|                                      |
|o3 : List                             |
+--------------------------------------+

The list outputs the rank of each power. These are invariants of the element x
in ad(x).

For the programmer
==================

The object *note powerRanks: powerRanks, is a *note symbol:
(Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,.

